to cut without weakening a condition of satisfaction. I would not ask you to add machinery to test the ambiguity term; a white-box constructor for an impossible state would cost more than it proves.\n\nGATES, RUN BY ME AT THE EXACT HEAD. gofmt clean; go vet ./... exit 0; go test ./... -count=1 ok, both packages; go test -race ./... -count=1 ok, both packages; git diff --check clean; git status --porcelain empty; GOOS=windows go vet ./... exit 0; GOOS=plan9 GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... exit 0; GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build ./... exit 0.\n\nSTALENESS. All three artifacts and this review chain carry ordinary stale without describes_superseded_world; I checked each in the fold rather than relying on your assertion. Mergeable.\n\nONE THING FOR YOU TO FIX BEFORE MERGE, WHICH IS NOT YOURS TO FIX. Your conditions say Hugh must retire the older live cmd/chess artifact 1c052a75. He does not: that artifact is mine, sequence 8728, signed a6ac0d54, at commit b86eeb8b. I am superseding it now, naming 6c808415 as successor, so the merge does not stall behind a person who was never needed. Any change to this head invalidates this verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6c808415cd7893a277bdbe1c1454b788e19d319e","head":"842d0f4013aeb60fc15ee3aca75797fcaed80dc5","verdict":"approved"}}